    {
      "id": "claim_1f10d23ab027450b855dc5ad2b9a0cd5",
      "statement": "STABILITY_TODOS.md is a 550-line stability investigation dated 2026-11-14 at v0.6.2 covering all 25 Python files in src/lumux/, written against a user report of instability on a CachyOS (Arch-based) Wayland desktop; its stated big picture is that the app mixes a sync thread, GStreamer streaming threads, a portal D-Bus connection, a requests session, an openssl subprocess, and GTK's main loop, and almost every instability class comes from blocking or thread-affine work done on the wrong thread.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://STABILITY_TODOS.md#L1-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f9f731e91fc69f38ef09b1c0fe9e00fd7f2d546575d33ec25574084d1c9a546c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_17efb4121f4843f092885bbaafd44eb5",
      "statement": "P0 item 1: BridgeClient's 5 s per-request timeout combined with synchronous call sites on the GTK main thread (startup reading-mode auto-activation, switch_to_video's REST activate + DTLS connect, the 1 s-delayed _finish_switch_to_reading with one PUT per light, opening Settings, wizard post-auth connect) produces 20-30 s main-loop freezes on a dead bridge, long enough for the Gio.Application D-Bus name to be marked unresponsive or lost; the proposed fix generalizes the existing get_bridge_status_async worker-thread + GLib.idle_add pattern to all bridge/DTLS operations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://STABILITY_TODOS.md#L26-L61",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c9922eaaf00d00607f3f6a83144b1caac98e5ed288e657933dca85578481015:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7926aed7876147b082d67f6805e5ffbe",
      "statement": "P0 item 2: pydbus is explicitly not thread-safe, yet the portal SessionBus is created on the Sync worker thread (capture._setup_portal_session) while session.Close() runs on the main thread during Stop/close/quit, causing a ~25 s D-Bus hang or undefined behavior and possibly leaving the session open; the proposed fix is a dedicated portal worker thread with a running GLib.MainLoop where all session operations are enqueued via queue.Queue.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://STABILITY_TODOS.md#L62-L93",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:411315c87b3225e5cf263280fc5590cbae1c53ad3c308902306c8ecc107d43b2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_be83b35f4b684960a3b9594a5ff58bf2",
      "statement": "P0 item 3: GStreamer bus.add_signal_watch() is called from the sync thread, whose while/time.sleep loop never iterates a GLib context, so _on_pipeline_error never fires and the converter-fallback machinery is dead code; when the portal kills the stream (permission revocation, monitor sleep/wake, resolution change) capture() keeps returning the last frame forever — lights freeze, UI shows Syncing, nothing recovers until app restart.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://STABILITY_TODOS.md#L94-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b59314133e5a1899998d67deed3913fef899f4eacdc4c0c94b18224bf7190a3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_72abd61cf56a4960a7c63d20224d1f64",
      "statement": "P0 item 4: pipeline lifecycle is unsynchronized between threads — app_context.apply_settings (main thread) can call _restart_pipeline while the sync thread is inside _start_pipeline, both mutating _pipeline/_appsink/_pipeline_running with no lock and calling Gst.Pipeline.set_state() from two threads, which GStreamer does not support (intermittent crashes/segfaults); the stop path also drops _latest_frame without taking the frame lock. The fix serializes all lifecycle operations on one thread with the sync loop only setting a flag.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://STABILITY_TODOS.md#L125-L145",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee1020884e19572b1ecbf7943b49480123d20e52211ca914399803ffc9130495:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_699aca64be494339b01c7c2c5442c262",
      "statement": "P0 item 5 (reproduced headlessly): turn_off() within 1 s of switch_to_reading() re-lights the room — turn_off clears the _reading_activation_pending flag but cannot cancel the already-scheduled GLib timeout, and _finish_switch_to_reading's interruption check passes because turn_off has set the mode to OFF, so reading mode activates ~1 s after an explicit off; the repro shows mode OFF immediately after turn_off and READING 1.5 s later, and the proposed fix stores the GLib source id and calls source_remove() in turn_off/switch_to_video.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://STABILITY_TODOS.md#L146-L177",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e2d02d5e5433216e1f8c57c052fc59c70096782a235ca91045bc99521fee98f5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f5119ed086894e7e93fb081fa14f779f",
      "statement": "P0 item 6 (reproduced headlessly): settings save() writes settings.json in place (non-atomic) and load is strict all-or-nothing — a SIGKILL mid-write persists a partly-defaults config (save runs on every sync start via the restore-token callback), and a file containing one unknown key fails HueSettings(**data) unpacking so the entire file is dropped (bridge_ip reverted to ''); the proposed fix is an os.replace atomic write with a .bak fallback plus tolerant per-field filtering via dataclass fields.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://STABILITY_TODOS.md#L178-L205",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:289a744ce4b3d625b77889e8f2b581eb3e55830cffe1e3e1e980a1a05178d728:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_451f5f0ae2424bf19f617ab30f15a82e",
      "statement": "P1 items include: the EntertainmentStream message buffer assumes a 36-char config ID so a non-UUID zone ID misaligns channel packing and a caught struct.error is printed 30x/s with sync silently dead (reproduced); HueBridge.create_user() ignores its max_retries/timeout parameters despite a docstring promising backoff; app/tray icon paths point at files that do not exist; DTLS via openssl s_client has undrained stdout/stderr pipes (64 KB fill stalls DTLS), a zombie process, and no reconnection; one requests.Session is shared across main/async/wizard threads and is not thread-safe; apply_settings() leaves a stale EntertainmentStream in both consumers when streaming is disabled; 'ready' is a dead status-card state; refresh_devices() re-runs on every brightness slider release; and the sync loop's error handler swallows tracebacks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://STABILITY_TODOS.md#L206-L370",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e94e0a59f4789337b7efa2cf309f8ce057aa23dd8860612fb49c3d6cda4b26b:"
        }
